8,Omurano Language and the Omurano Indian Tribe (Maina),http://www.native-languages.org/omurano.htm,"Omurano was a language of Peru, which no longer is spoken today. There are few records of the Omurano language remaining, and its relationships to other Anazonian languages are uncertain. Some linguists believe it was a language isolate, unrelated to any other language.",Omurano,Language isolate
9,OLAC resources in and about the Omurano language,http://www.language-archives.org/language/omu,"ONLINELINGUIST List Resources for Omurano. Damir Cavar, Director of Linguist List (editor); Malgorzata E. Cavar, Director of Linguist List (editor). 2017-09-27. The LINGUIST List (www.linguistlist.org). oai:linguistlist.org:lang_omu · ONLINESmall language families and isolates in Peru.",Omurano,Language isolate
